<title>JAPAN: Tobishima's shares soar on hopes of debt relief.</title>
<headline>Tobishima's shares soar on hopes of debt relief.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tobishima Corp's shares soared on Wednesday afternoon on signs that its debt restructuring plan will soon be accepted by its creditors, brokers said.</p>
<p>The construction firm said that it believes all of its creditor financial institutions will eventually agree to its debt-relief plan.</p>
<p>By 0345 GMT, Tobishima's shares had gained 27.27 percent or 57 yen to 266, making the firm the largest percentage gainer on the first section of the bourse. It was also the most active stock with a turnover of 7.231 million.</p>
</text>
